The tools in this directory are ported from aipmy/msm8916-openwrt
(https://github.com/aipmy/msm8916-openwrt), commit
178f15bfbff5511be03e4a048c1c551470bf587b (2026-11-24), where they
are OpenWrt packages. Only the userspace programs and shell scripts
are vendored here; the OpenWrt package Makefiles are replaced by
aipmy.mk, and the procd init scripts by the OpenRC scripts in
openrc/ and the systemd units in systemd/.

Licenses (per upstream package metadata):
  BSD-3-Clause: qcom-time-daemon, ats-probe, bt-spp, bt-ssp-guard
  GPL-2.0-only: diag-bind, diag-efs (diag_efs), diag-logtool
                (diag_logtool), reboot-edl (reboot-mode)

Not ported: reboot-edl's unbuilt alternate sources (reboot-edl.c,
reboot-dload.c, reboot-mode.c — upstream only builds
reboot-mode-raw plus the reboot-mode script), and the LuCI apps.

Round 2 (2026-11-26) adds clean-room adaptations of further aipmy
features, reimplemented for this builder's NetworkManager /
systemd / OpenRC stack (no UCI, no procd, no web UI), in
scripts/ + src/diag_nv.c + configs/failsafe/button-watch.c:
qcom-carrier-autocfg (as carrier-autocfg; upstream's MCFG
activation stays disabled, as upstream itself disabled it, and
the MBN blobs are NOT vendored), change-imei, the modem-care
services (modem-bearer-watchdog, sim-hotplug, modem-led-monitor,
wifi-led-monitor, lan-speed), modem-bandlock, himi-ok-guard, and
a failsafe button monitor.  diag_nv is an original implementation
of the documented DIAG NV_READ_F/NV_WRITE_F commands providing
the interface of upstream's prebuilt diag_nv.bin (whose source is
not published).  Licenses: GPL-2.0-only for the round-2 items
(upstream base-files and qcom-carrier-autocfg are GPL-2.0-only).
